Relevant columns & why they matter  

• Match."season": group‑by key to calculate per‑season statistics.  
• Match."home_team_api_id": team id for the home side; use in joins / aggregations.  
• Match."away_team_api_id": team id for the away side; use in joins / aggregations.  
• Match."home_team_goal": number of goals scored by the home side in a match.  
• Match."away_team_goal": number of goals scored by the away side in a match.  
• Team."team_api_id": primary key when joining to Match.*_team_api_id.  
• Team."team_long_name": human‑readable team name (optional for display).  

Typical conditions you will need  

• WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL (or the same for away) – filter out unfinished matches.  
• JOIN "Match"  ON  Team."team_api_id" = Match."home_team_api_id" (or away) – to get team names.  
• GROUP BY "season", "team_api_id" – to accumulate goals in one season.  
• MAX(total_goals) OVER (PARTITION BY "team_api_id") – to find the highest‑scoring season of each club.  

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from the very simple to the final one that returns the median of the “highest season‑goals” for every team.

```sql
-- 1) See which seasons exist in the data set
SELECT DISTINCT "season"
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;

-- 2) Peek at raw goal counts for a handful of matches
SELECT "season",
       "home_team_api_id",
       "away_team_api_id",
       "home_team_goal",
       "away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 3) Look at team ids and their long names
SELECT DISTINCT "team_api_id",
       "team_long_name"
FROM "Team"
LIMIT 20;

-- 4) Example: matches where team 9987 played at home
SELECT "season",
       "home_team_goal" AS "goals_scored"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_team_api_id" = 9987
LIMIT 20;

-- 5) Example: matches where team 9987 played away
SELECT "season",
       "away_team_goal" AS "goals_scored"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "away_team_api_id" = 9987
LIMIT 20;

-- 6) Aggregate home‑side goals per team per season
SELECT "season",
       "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
       SUM("home_team_goal") AS "home_goals_season"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "season", "home_team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;

-- 7) Aggregate away‑side goals per team per season
SELECT "season",
       "away_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
       SUM("away_team_goal") AS "away_goals_season"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "away_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "season", "away_team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;

-- 8) Combine home and away to get TOTAL goals per team per season
WITH home AS (
    SELECT "season",
           "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
           SUM("home_team_goal") AS "goals"
    FROM "Match"
    WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "season", "home_team_api_id"
),
away AS (
    SELECT "season",
           "away_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
           SUM("away_team_goal") AS "goals"
    FROM "Match"
    WHERE "away_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "season", "away_team_api_id"
)
SELECT "season",
       "team_api_id",
       SUM("goals") AS "total_goals_season"
FROM (
    SELECT * FROM home
    UNION ALL
    SELECT * FROM away
)
GROUP BY "season", "team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;

-- 9) For each team, find its highest‑scoring season
WITH team_season_goals AS (
    SELECT "season",
           "team_api_id",
           SUM("goals") AS "total_goals"
    FROM (
        SELECT "season",
               "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
               "home_team_goal" AS "goals"
        FROM "Match"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "season",
               "away_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
               "away_team_goal" AS "goals"
        FROM "Match"
    )
    GROUP BY "season", "team_api_id"
)
SELECT "team_api_id",
       MAX("total_goals") AS "highest_season_goals"
FROM team_season_goals
GROUP BY "team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;

-- 10) FINAL: median of the “highest season goals” across all teams
WITH team_season_goals AS (
    SELECT "season",
           "team_api_id",
           SUM("goals") AS "total_goals"
    FROM (
        SELECT "season",
               "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
               "home_team_goal" AS "goals"
        FROM "Match"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "season",
               "away_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
               "away_team_goal" AS "goals"
        FROM "Match"
    )
    GROUP BY "season", "team_api_id"
),
team_best_season AS (
    SELECT "team_api_id",
           MAX("total_goals") AS "max_goals"
    FROM team_season_goals
    GROUP BY "team_api_id"
),
ordered AS (
    SELECT "max_goals",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY "max_goals") AS rn,
           COUNT(*) OVER () AS cnt
    FROM team_best_season
)
SELECT AVG("max_goals") AS "median_highest_season_goals"
FROM ordered
WHERE rn IN ( (cnt + 1) / 2, (cnt + 2) / 2 );
```

Each successive query helps you understand or build toward the final calculation of the median number of goals scored in the best season of every team.
